@  DRAFT (T-313): the CAPTAIN is DAVID, the player's brother (the user, 2026-09-26) -- fond of boats, and still seasick.
SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_CaptainIFeelSeasick::
    .string "DAVID: Oh… it's you.\p"
    .string "Don't tell MOM. The captain of\n"
    .string "the S.S. ANNE is… urrp… seasick.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_RubbedCaptainsBack::
    .string "{PLAYER} rubbed DAVID's back!\p"
    .string "Rub-rub…\n"
    .string "Rub-rub…$"

@  DRAFT (T-586, the user 2026-11-17): the book, the choice, and the porthole.
SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_HelpsABit::
    .string "DAVID: Thanks. That helps a bit.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_BackToTheBook::
    .string "DAVID went back to his book.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_StillAtIt::
    .string "DAVID: …Still seasick.\n"
    .string "Still reading.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_EveryStep::
    .string "DAVID: It has every step in it.\n"
    .string "It never says where to look.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_KeepReading::
    .string "DAVID: You're right. One more\n"
    .string "chapter…\p"
    .string "…urrp.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_LooksOut::
    .string "DAVID put the book down and\n"
    .string "looked out the porthole.\p"
    .string "Far off, the sea met the sky\n"
    .string "in one long line that held still.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_ThereTheWholeTime::
    .string "DAVID: It was there the whole\n"
    .string "time.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_Compass::
    .string "DAVID: One more thing.\p"
    .string "I can see where I'm going now.\n"
    .string "You'll need this more than I do.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_ObtainedCompass::
    .string "{PLAYER} obtained the COMPASS\n"
    .string "from DAVID!$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_ThankYouHaveHMForCut::
    .string "DAVID: …Better. Thank you.\p"
    .string "I've loved boats since before you\n"
    .string "could walk. The sea still does this.\p"
    .string "Here, take this. It clears what\n"
    .string "stands in your way.\p"
    .string "I never need it at sea.\p"
    .string "Teach it to your DAEMONS and you\n"
    .string "can use PRUNE any time.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_ObtainedHM01FromCaptain::
    .string "{PLAYER} obtained DRIVER01\n"
    .string "from DAVID!$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_ExplainCut::
    .string "Using PRUNE, you can chop down\n"
    .string "small trees.\p"
    .string "Why not try it with the trees\n"
    .string "around ARDOR CITY?$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_SSAnneWillSetSailSoon::
    .string "DAVID: The S.S. ANNE sails soon.\p"
    .string "Call MOM for me, would you?\n"
    .string "She'll say I never do.\p"
    .string "She's right.$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_YouHaveNoRoomForThis::
    .string "Oh, no!\n"
    .string "You have no room for this!$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_YuckShouldntHaveLooked::
    .string "Yuck!\n"
    .string "Shouldn't have looked!$"

SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_HowToConquerSeasickness::
    .string "How to Conquer Seasickness…\n"
    .string "Every line is underlined.$"


@  DRAFT (T-10): what gives the singing fir its key is still the user's; this is the proposal.
SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_BandsSheet::
    .string "DAVID: And this. The band leaves\n"
    .string "it on the piano every voyage.\p"
    .string "A key and no tune. They say the\n"
    .string "tune is somewhere in ARDOR.\p"
    .string "I've never found it.\n"
    .string "Maybe you will.$"

@ T-401 (the user, 2026-10-15): every page is filed in the same words.
SSAnne_CaptainsOffice_Text_SheetIntoNotebook::
    .string "{PLAYER} copied it into the\n"
    .string "NOTEBOOK.$"
